%% Mermaid sequence diagram: Inbound call flow
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Caller
    participant T as Telephony (Twilio/SIP)
    participant R as Realtime Orchestrator (WebRTC/WS)
    participant STT as STT Provider
    participant DM as Dialog Manager (LLM)
    participant TTS as ElevenLabs TTS
    participant DB as Storage (S3/DB)
    participant App as Mobile App (UI)

    C->>T: Dial business E.164
    T->>R: Establish media session (SIP↔WebRTC)
    R->>DB: Start recording (S3 pre-signed upload)
    R->>STT: Stream audio (opus/pcm16)
    STT-->>R: transcript.partial (seq, startMs, text, confidence)
    R-->>App: transcript.partial (WS)
    par Intent + early response
        R->>DM: Context + partial transcript
        DM-->>R: Short ack or reply text
        R->>TTS: Stream TTS request
        TTS-->>R: tts.chunk (first bytes <150ms)
        R-->>T: RTP audio chunk
        T-->>C: Play audio
    and Duplex with barge-in
        C-->>R: User speaking (VAD barge-in)
        R-->>TTS: Pause/stop current TTS
        R->>STT: Continue streaming user speech
    end
    loop Turn-taking
        STT-->>R: transcript.final (seq, text)
        R->>DB: Persist segment
        R->>DM: Update dialog state
        DM-->>R: Next reply
        R->>TTS: Stream TTS
        TTS-->>R: tts.chunk...
        R-->>T: Audio...
        T-->>C: Audio...
    end
    R->>DB: Finalize transcript, notes, analytics
    R-->>App: call.ended + links
    T-->>C: Hangup

    Note over R,DM: Predictive start allowed with partial intents
    Note over R,TTS: Cache common greetings to reduce TTFB
